<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <key>com.apple.security.get-task-allow</key>
    <true/>
    <!--
      An `com.apple.security.application-groups` entitlement was tried here
      (2026-08-15) to share the Quick Look "customize the default playback
      speed" preference with this app's own Settings window, so it could be
      set in one place and read by the (mandatorily sandboxed) Quick Look
      extension. Reverted: this machine has zero code-signing identities
      configured (`security find-identity -v -p codesigning` returns none,
      no Development Team) and Xcode refuses to build ANY target declaring
      an app-group entitlement without one — "entitlements that require
      signing with a development certificate." App groups need a real
      (even free/Personal-Team) Apple ID signed into Xcode; ad-hoc "Sign to
      Run Locally" alone isn't enough. Revisit if that's ever set up —
      `QuickLookPlaybackPreferences` (CinePlayerCore) already has the
      suite-name-based storage ready to go, just currently pointed at
      `UserDefaults.standard` instead.
    -->
</dict>
</plist>
